cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Iterated Digit-Sum Power Maps: A Lower Bound Theorem, an Exact Basin Density Law, and the Oscillation of Intra-Signature Basin Splits"
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper and, where relevant, the software."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Martins
    given-names: Alex
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-28"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - discrete dynamical systems
  - digit-sum functions
  - generalized happy numbers
  - modular arithmetic
  - attractor basins
  - natural density
  - power digraphs
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and verification suite for the family of discrete
  dynamical systems f_{k,b}(n) = S_b(n^k), where S_b is the base-b digit-sum
  function. Provides the exhaustive attractor/basin miner over the rigorous
  trapping region, the modular power map with closed forms for both the
  periodic-point count and the cycle count, the Monte-Carlo measurement of the
  intra-signature basin split, and a parameter-free model of its oscillation.
